{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"cd9c7ff4-9f64-4dbc-a94e-ba88be9d37ac","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The caching issue has been resolved by separating the system prompt into two blocks: a cached block for static instructions and an uncached block for dynamic athlete context.\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Root Cause**:\n   In [bot.py](file:///tmp/h-RPnDYH/bot.py#L130-L135), [`build_system`](file:///tmp/h-RPnDYH/bot.py#L130) previously combined [`INSTRUCTIONS`](file:///tmp/h-RPnDYH/bot.py#L74) and [`athlete_context`](file:///tmp/h-RPnDYH/bot.py#L117) into a single text block marked with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`. Whenever `save_fact` appended a memory item, the text of this unified block changed. Because Claude prompt caching uses prefix matching, altering the combined block invalidated the cached prompt prefix, forcing subsequent calls to recreate the cache at full token cost.\n\n2. **Fix**:\n   Updated [`build_system`](file:///tmp/h-RPnDYH/bot.py#L130-L135) to return two content blocks:\n   - A static block containing [`INSTRUCTIONS`](file:///tmp/h-RPnDYH/bot.py#L74) marked with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`.\n   - A dynamic block containing [`athlete_context(a, today)`](file:///tmp/h-RPnDYH/bot.py#L117) without cache control.\n\n3. **Documentation**:\n   Detailed the issue and changes in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-RPnDYH/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":278.063331,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":161016,"output_tokens":23584,"thinking_tokens":21143,"cache_read_tokens":989052,"total_tokens":184600}}}
